# 8. 180-DAY EW ELIGIBILITY VALIDATION

Customers are eligible to apply for Extended Warranty within 180 days from the actual Ship Date.

The eligibility calculation must use the **Ship Date**, not the SO Date.

### Calculation

Days Since Shipment = Current Date - Ship Date

### Eligibility rules

| Condition | Result |
|---|---|
| 0–180 days since shipment | Eligible |
| More than 180 days | Ineligible |
| Missing Ship Date | Requires Review |
| Future Ship Date | Requires Review |

Treat day 180 as eligible unless an authorized administrator changes the business rule.

The 180-day eligibility period must be configurable in Settings.

### Eligibility display

Show:

- Ship Date
- Current Date
- Days Since Shipment
- Days Remaining
- Eligibility Status

Use clear status indicators:

- Eligible
- Ineligible
- Requires Review
- Exception Approved

Do not allow an ineligible order to generate a normal quotation.

An Administrator may authorize an exception if the business permits it.

Every exception must record:

- User who authorized it
- Date and time
- Reason
- Original eligibility result
- Authorized eligibility outcome

The exception must be visible in the quotation and Activity Logs.

Perform eligibility validation on the backend using the configured business timezone and date rules.

